    "https://www.schooljobs.com/careers/enmu/jobs/5469765/network-specialist": {
      "title": "Network Specialist",
      "description": "Main Campus - Portales | Employment Opportunities For full functionality of this page it is necessary to enable JavaScript. \n        Here are the instructions how to enable JavaScript in your web browser Network Specialist | Employment Opportunities page has loaded. Network Specialist | Employment Opportunities page has loaded. Click here or press any key to continue. Main Campus - Portales Menu Main Campus - Portales Sign In Don't have an account? Create one . Already have an account? Sign In . User profile dropdown menu for Username Applications Inbox Profile Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Applications Inbox Profile Go to Background Investigation Account Sign Out After clicking on this link you will be logged out and the page will be reloaded. Welcome! Thanks for creating an account. Employment Opportunities powered by NEOGOV ® Need this page in another language? You can translate this page using your browser's built-in translation feature. Tip: In Chrome or Edge, right-click anywhere on the page and select \"Translate to [Language].\" Network Specialist Print Apply ﻿ Network Specialist Salary Depends on Qualifications Location Main Campus - Portales, NM Job Type Full time permanent Job Number 2026-00149 Department Business Affairs Division Information Technology Services Opening Date 09/02/2026 Description Benefits Position Overview Position Summary The Network Specialist is a member of the Information Technology Services (ITS) Infrastructure team responsible for maintaining, monitoring, securing, and enhancing Eastern New Mexico University’s wired and wireless network infrastructure. This position provides technical support for enterprise network services across multiple campuses by installing, configuring, troubleshooting, and documenting network systems, and by contributing to infrastructure projects that improve reliability, security, and performance. Under the general supervision of the Manager of Client and Network Services, the Network Specialist provides operational support for the University’s network infrastructure, including Cisco switching, routing, wireless networking, firewalls, VPN connectivity, network monitoring, and related services. Working collaboratively with other ITS teams and campus departments, the Network Specialist helps ensure reliable, secure, and resilient network services while developing and applying broader technical expertise in enterprise networking technologies. Requirements Duties and Responsibilities: Configure, maintain, install, and optimize Cisco switches, routers, wireless access points, controllers, and related network infrastructure. Analyze complex network infrastructure issues, evaluate alternative technical solutions, and exercise independent judgment in determining appropriate corrective actions to maintain network availability, security, performance, and reliability Monitor network health and performance using enterprise monitoring systems to proactively identify and resolve issues. Diagnose and resolve complex wired and wireless connectivity problems for faculty, staff, students, and campus departments. Evaluate perimeter firewalls, VPN services, network security appliances, and access control technologies; implement approved security controls and recommend improvements to strengthen network security Configure and maintain VLANs, spanning tree, trunking, DHCP relay, and other Layer 2 and Layer 3 networking technologies. Configure, implement, administer, and maintain network authentication systems, including Cisco ISE, RADIUS, and 802.1X. Evaluate and troubleshoot campus fiber and copper network infrastructure, coordinate physical-layer repairs and installations, and verify connectivity and performance Plan and perform network equipment upgrades, firmware updates, backups, and configuration management. Maintain configuration backups for critical network infrastructure and participate in the development and testing of network disaster recovery and business continuity procedures. Develop and maintain comprehensive technical documentation, including network architecture diagrams, configuration standards, inventories, IP addressing plans, security configurations, and operational procedures Participate in the planning, design, evaluation, and implementation of network expansion, refresh, and modernization projects. Evaluate network performance, reliability, security, and capacity, and make technical recommendations regarding infrastructure, configurations, technologies, and standards to improve enterprise network services. Work closely with Systems, Client Support, Help Desk, Smart Classroom, and Telecommunications personnel to resolve infrastructure issues. Participate in an on-call rotation and respond to network outages or emergencies outside normal business hours when necessary. Regular and predictable attendance required Perform other related duties as assigned. Minimum Job Requirements: Bachelor’s degree in Information Technology, Computer Science, Cybersecurity, Networking, or a related field, and two years of related experience; or an equivalent combination of education, certifications, and directly related professional experience is required. Valid driver’s license. Ability to obtain a Cisco Certified Network Associate (CCNA) certification within one year of employment if not already held. Preferred Qualifications: Current Cisco Certified Network Associate (CCNA) certification or higher. Two or more years of experience supporting enterprise networking environments. Experience administering Cisco Catalyst switching and enterprise wireless infrastructure. Experience with Cisco Firepower, Meraki, or comparable enterprise networking platforms. Experience with Cisco Identity Services Engine (ISE), RADIUS, or network access control (NAC). Experience with enterprise network monitoring and management platforms. Experience working in higher education, healthcare, government, or another multi-building, distributed environment. Knowledge of Zero Trust networking principles and network security best practices. Experience supporting Layer 3 routing protocols, including OSPF. Experience with IPv6 implementation or administration. Experience performing packet capture and network traffic analysis. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities: Strong understanding of TCP/IP networking and the OSI model. Working knowledge of Layer 2 switching technologies, including VLANs, STP/RSTP, EtherChannel, 802.1Q trunking, and port security. Working knowledge of Layer 3 technologies, including static routing, inter-VLAN routing, access control lists, and IP routing fundamentals. Understanding of IPv4 and IPv6 addressing and subnetting. Familiarity with enterprise wireless networking technologies. Knowledge of network security technologies, including firewalls, VPN, IDS/IPS, network access control (NAC), and multifactor authentication (MFA). Ability to install, configure, maintain, and troubleshoot enterprise network infrastructure. Ability to diagnose complex network problems using packet captures, network analysis tools, and structured troubleshooting techniques. Ability to create and maintain accurate technical documentation, including network diagrams, configuration records, and operational procedures. Ability to prioritize multiple assignments and manage work effectively in a dynamic environment. Strong written, verbal, and interpersonal communication skills. Ability to work independently and collaboratively as part of a team. Commitment to providing responsive customer service and continuous professional development. Working Conditions Physical Demand and Working Conditions: Work is performed in the office, classroom, telecommunications room, data center, and outdoor environments. Work may involve confined spaces, ceilings, dust, poor ventilation, noise, vibration, rooftops, and varying weather conditions. Ability to lift and carry up to 50 pounds and frequently climb ladders and use hand tools. Occasional evening and weekend work is required for scheduled maintenance and emergency response. Essential Functions: [As defined under the Americans with Disabilities Act, these include the aforementioned duties and responsibilities, minimum job requirements, knowledge, skills, and abilities, as well as physical demands and working conditions. This is not necessarily an all-inclusive listing.] Additional Information Application Review Date: Condition of Employment: Must pass a pre-employment background check. Electronic Application Instructions: Electronic applications should be submitted through the \"Apply\" link at the top of this page. Please attach the following required documents to your electronic application: Required Documents: Please ensure that you attach all required documents, even if you have applied for other positions at ENMU, as the committee does not have access to those records. Letter of interest Resume Contact information for three references (blind or off-list reference checks may be conducted on finalists) Transcripts (unofficial for application purposes) Equal Employment Opportunity /Title IX/IPRA. Eastern New Mexico University does not discriminate on the basis of race, color, national origin, religion, sex (including pregnancy, gender identity, and sexual orientation), age, disability, genetic information, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected under federal, state, or local laws. If a reasonable accommodation is needed to participate in the job application or interview process, or to perform essential job functions, please contact the Office of Human Resources at (575) 562-2115. New Mexico is an open records state; therefore, ENMU complies with the Inspection of Public Records Act, NMSA 1978, Chapter 14, Article 2, from the Office of the New Mexico Attorney General. Any concerns regarding sex discrimination should be addressed to the Title IX Coordinator at either titleix.coordinator@enmu.eu , (575) 562-2235, or Curry Hall Office 127, 1500 S Avenue K, Portales, NM 88130. Requests for inspection of public records should be sent to planning.analysis@enmu.edu . For any other inquiries, please contact Human Resources at (575) 562-2115 or e-mail ENMU.HRrecruiter@enmu.edu . ENMU uses E-Verify to confirm the employment eligibility of all newly hired employees. To learn more about E-Verify, including your rights and responsibilities, please visit www.dhs.gov/E-Verify. Insurance Insurance for Eastern New Mexico University is offered through the New Mexico Public Schools Insurance Authority . High coverage and low coverage options are offered for medical and dental insurance so employees can choose the plan that’s right for them. Health insurance is offered through both Blue Cross and Blue Shield of New Mexico and the Presbyterian Health Plan Dental insurance is offered through United Concordia , Delta Dental , and Blue Cross Blue Shield Dental Vision insurance is offered through Davis Vision . Life insurance is offered through Standard Life Insurance Company and UNUM Life Insurance Company . Retirement Eastern New Mexico University participates with the New Mexico Educational Retirement Board (NMERB) , Social Security , and Medicare . The University also offers supplemental retirement plans. 403b and 457b plans are available through TIAA/CREF , AIG VALIC , Roth 403b and 457b plans are also available through TIAA/CREF . Paid Time Off Full time exempt employees accrue 14.66 hours of annual leave and 14 hours of medical leave per month. Employee Educational Assistance Plan Eastern New Mexico University offers a tuition waiver for regular employees and retirees. This program waives the tuition for three courses (up to nine credit hours) per semester. Employees' spouses or children may be eligible to use the tuition waiver during any semester that it is not being used by the employee. Employer Eastern New Mexico University Address 1500 S. Ave. K, Station 21 Portales, New Mexico, 88130 Phone 575-562-2115 Website http://www.enmu.edu Apply Please verify your email address Verify Email Main Campus - Portales Account Privacy Policy Terms Of Use Accessibility Statement Privacy Settings Copyright © 2026 Do not sell my personal information × For California residents, and to the extent NEOGOV sells your personal information as the term “sell” is defined under the California Consumer Privacy Act, you have the right to opt-out of the sale of your personal information by us to third parties at any time. This setting only applies to registered account holders that have opted-in for an Access Membership. If you wish to opt-out click follow these steps: Log into your Job Seeker Profile Click your name in the upper right-hand corner Select Account Settings Select the Preferences section Click the Edit button next to Access Membership Switch Toggle to off Click Save If you do not have a registered account this setting does not apply, however, you can review your right on our privacy policy . If you require further assistance, please email privacy@neogov.com × Accessibility Statement At Governmentjobs.com, Inc. d/b/a NEOGOV, we recognize the importance of making our products\n                    and services accessible to all individuals, including those with disabilities, and are continually\n                    working to improve the experience for all users. Commitment to Accessibility We are committed to following best practices, including the Web Content Accessibility Guidelines\n                    (WCAG) 2.1, Level AA, to the extent feasible, however, we do not warrant compliance with these\n                    standards or any other accessibility standards. We are continually enhancing our platforms to\n                    ensure greater accessibility, and we actively seek out opportunities to improve accessibility features. Ongoing Enhancements Accessibility is an ongoing effort, and we are regularly updating our technology, services, and content\n                    to address accessibility barriers. Our team is dedicated to identifying areas for improvement and\n                    making enhancements that allow all users, regardless of their abilities, to fully engage with our\n                    services. Feedback and Assistance We value feedback from our users. If you encounter any accessibility barriers while using our services\n                    or have suggestions on how we can improve, please reach out to us at accessibility@neogov.com.\n                    We will make every effort to resolve any concerns and consider alternative options where possible. Thank you for choosing NEOGOV. We remain dedicated to improving accessibility and creating an\n                    inclusive experience for all. Employment Opportunities Main Campus - Portales Menu Close Menu Employment Opportunities Main Campus - Portales Roswell Campus Ruidoso Campus Job Categories Help & Support Translate Support Job Application Job Details Applying as: | Support Close Close Cancel Clear SIGN Save We've updated our Privacy Policy and Terms of Use. Please, read and accept changes. Effective date: August 19, 2025 NEOGOV PRIVACY POLICY Contents 1. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. 2. Where We Are a Service Provider. 3. Personal Data We Collect About You and Why. 4. Cookies and Similar Tracking Technologies. 5. Online Analytics and Advertising. 6. Information We Disclose. 7. International Users. 8. Your Data Rights and Choices. 9. Notice to California Residents. 10. Your Rights and Control under EU GDPR. 11. Data Security and Integrity. 12. Retention and Removal. 13. Right to Revise. 14. Contact Details. 15. Privacy Contacts. Introduction; Scope of this Policy. The purpose of this Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) is to describe how we collect, use, store, protect, and disclose personal data online and offline either via our websites or related applications. This Policy applies to personal data